type: software
title: "Replication package for: Selecting In-Progress Delivery Routes for Resequencing under Limited Intervention Capacity"
authors:
  - family-names: "Nguyễn"
    given-names: "Nhật Thanh"
    affiliation: "International University, Vietnam National University, Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam"
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DeckardShaw31/Selecting-In-Progress-Delivery-Routes-for-Resequencing-under-Limited-Intervention-Capacity"
keywords:
  - last-mile delivery
  - real-time intervention
  - capacity-limited triage
  - priority rules
  - stochastic routing
  - pre-specified simulation
abstract: >-
  Code, pre-specification documents and derived results for a study of which in-progress
  delivery routes a dispatcher should resequence when only a few can be changed at a time.
  It compares behind-schedule triage with risk triage, a deterministic projection of the
  remaining promises, and probabilistic forecasts, on real Amazon route structures and on
  observed outcomes from Norway/Denmark and five Chinese cities.
